       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>2.2 
      </section-number>
      <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>References
     </subsection>
     <text-unit xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
        id="ID.0023"
        rolemaps-to="Part"
       >
      <text xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
         id="ID.0024"
         xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
         Layout:TextAlign="Justify"
         rolemaps-to="P"
        >
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>The class makes various changes to the way that references are handled. The class loads natbib, and also the appropriate bibliography style. References can be made using the normal method; the citation should be placed before any punctuation, as the class will move it if using a superscript citation style.
       <Span xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
          id="ID.0025"
          xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
          Layout:TextPosition="Sup"
         >
        <Reference xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn"
           id="ID.0026"
          >
          <?References objects="1" ?>
         <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>1
        </Reference>
        <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>–
        <Reference xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn"
           id="ID.0027"
          >
          <?References objects="2" ?>
         <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>4
        </Reference>
       </Span>
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?> The use of natbib allows the use of the various citation commands of that package: 
       <Reference xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn"
          id="ID.0028"
         >
         <?References objects="3" ?>
        <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>Abernethy et al.
       </Reference>
       <Span xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
          id="ID.0029"
          xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
          Layout:TextPosition="Sup"
         >
       </Span>
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?> have shown something, in 
       <Reference xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn"
          id="ID.0030"
         >
         <?References objects="4" ?>
        <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>1999
       </Reference>
       <Span xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
          id="ID.0031"
          xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
          Layout:TextPosition="Sup"
         >
       </Span>
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>, or as given by Ref.
       <Reference xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn"
          id="ID.0032"
         >
         <?References objects="1" ?>
        <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>1
       </Reference>
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>. Long lists of authors will be automatically truncated in most article formats, but not in supplementary information or reviews.
       <Span xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
          id="ID.0033"
          xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
          Layout:TextPosition="Sup"
         >
        <Reference xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn"
           id="ID.0034"
          >
          <?References objects="5" ?>
         <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>6
        </Reference>
       </Span>
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?> If you encounter problems with the citation macros, please check that your copy of natbib is up to date. The demonstration database file achemso-demo.bib shows how to complete entries correctly. Notice that “et al.” is auto-formatted using the \latin command.
      </text>
     </text-unit>
     <text-unit xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
        id="ID.0035"
        rolemaps-to="Part"
       >
      <text xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
         id="ID.0036"
         xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
         Layout:TextAlign="Justify"
         rolemaps-to="P"
        >
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>Multiple citations to be combined into a list can be given as a single cita
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>tion. This uses the mciteplus package.
       <Span xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
          id="ID.0037"
          xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
          Layout:TextPosition="Sup"
         >
        <Reference xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn"
           id="ID.0038"
          >
          <?References objects="6" ?>
         <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>7
        </Reference>
       </Span>
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?> Citations other than the first of the list should be indicated with a star. If the mciteplus package is not installed, the standard bibliography tools will still work but starred references will be ignored. Individual references can be referred to using \mciteSubRef: “ref. 7.c”.
      </text>
     </text-unit>
     <text-unit xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
        id="ID.0039"
        rolemaps-to="Part"
       >
      <text xmlns="https://www.latex-project.org/ns/dflt"
         id="ID.0040"
         xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
         Layout:TextAlign="Justify"
         rolemaps-to="P"
        >
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>The class also handles notes to be added to the bibliography. These should be given in place in the document.
       <Span xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
          id="ID.0041"
          xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
          Layout:TextPosition="Sup"
         >
        <Reference xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn"
           id="ID.0042"
          >
          <?References objects="7" ?>
         <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>8
        </Reference>
       </Span>
       <?MarkedContent page="1" ?> As with citations, the text should be placed before punctuation. A note is also generated if a citation has an optional note. This assumes that the whole work has already been cited: odd numbering will result if this is not the case.
       <Span xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf2/ssn"
          id="ID.0043"
          xmlns:Layout="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn/Layout"
          Layout:TextPosition="Sup"
         >
        <Reference xmlns="http://iso.org/pdf/ssn"
           id="ID.0044"
          >
          <?References objects="8" ?>
         <?MarkedContent page="1" ?>9
        </Reference>
       </Span>
      </text>
     </text-unit>
